# Go main server (`apps/server/arcyria-server`)

Fiber + GORM service between the Next.js app and the Python ELT server. **The
browser never calls ELT directly** — all authenticated product traffic goes
through this API.

## Stack

- **Web:** Fiber v2
- **DB:** GORM + Postgres (Supabase)
- **Queue:** pgmq (`internal/queue`)
- **Auth:** Supabase JWT on `/api/v1/*`; internal tokens (`X-ETL-Token`,
  `X-Callback-Token`) for ELT ↔ Go
- **Logs:** zerolog — never log credentials, tokens, or raw DSNs

## Layout (where to edit)

| Area | Path |
| --- | --- |
| HTTP routes & handlers | `internal/server/` |
| ELT HTTP client | `internal/elt/` |
| Queue worker / dispatch | `internal/server/dispatch.go`, `dispatch_incremental.go`, `staged_delivery.go` |
| Pipeline bundle / RunConfig builders | `internal/server/pipeline_bundle.go`, `pipeline_targets.go` |
| Callback from Python ELT | `internal/server/callback.go` |
| DB models | `internal/models/` |
| Entrypoint | `cmd/server/main.go` |

## ELT-specific files (keep in sync with Python contract)

When changing dispatch or callbacks, align with Pydantic models in the ELT
server (`apps/server/arcyria-elt/models/run_config.py`):

- `dispatch.go` / `dispatch_incremental.go` — build `selected_streams` as
  `SourceStreamConfig[]` (not raw `string[]`); `dbt_config.sql_models` with
  `dest_table` as `schema.table`.
- `pipeline_bundle.go` — `duckdbTableName`, `buildSourceStreamConfigs`,
  `buildStrictDBTSQLModels`.
- `staged_delivery.go` — disk guard (`ErrELTStagingDiskBusy`), `handleDiskBusy`,
  waiting + 30s re-queue.
- `callback.go` — persist `delivery_outputs`, `staging_size_bytes`,
  `dbt_models_run`, `no_pk_warnings` in run metadata.

## Product rules

- Destination contract is **destination-node-first** (`dest_schema`,
  `sql_models[].output_table`, final delivery as `schema.table`). See
  `apps/server/arcyria-server/README.md` for the short contract summary.
- Pipeline runs flow through **pgmq**, not ad-hoc HTTP from the frontend to ELT.

